]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Public Transport 🚌]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Price of public transport decreases]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Substitution effect: switch from cars 🚗 to buses 🚌]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Income effect: more money to spend 💸]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Let's consider an example. Suppose the price of public transportation decreases.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("The substitution effect might lead some people to switch from using their private cars to using public buses, because buses are now relatively cheaper.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("The income effect means that people now have more money to spend, because they're spending less on transportation. They might use this extra money to buy more of other goods and services.")
]
]

